>> title: Apple Pie
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: apple, pie, dessert, double crust, oven
>> counters: Diner, Bakery
>> aka: apple pie, double crust apple pie, deep dish apple pie, American apple pie
>> pairs-with: all-butter-pie-crust, french-vanilla-ice-cream
>> servings: 8
>> time: 6 hr
>> slack: narrow — cut warm, the filling runs out and the slice collapses, and there is no putting it back: the four hours of cooling is not optional

>> step: macerate 45 min, then drain the juice off
Macerate @Granny Smith apples{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; peeled, in 1/4-in slices), @Honeycrisp apples{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; peeled, in 1/4-in slices), @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g), @light brown sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @lemon juice{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}(2 g), @grated nutmeg{1/4%tsp} and @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g) together ~macerate{45%min}, then drain the juice into a saucepan.

>> step: reduce the juice to a syrup, 5 min
Reduce @&(~1)apple juice{} with @unsalted butter{1%Tbs}(14 g) over medium-high heat ~simmer{5%min}, to about 1/3 cup of syrup the colour of weak caramel.

>> step: toss the apples back through it
Toss @&(~1)apple syrup and slices{} with @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(16 g) until every slice is slick.

>> step: fill, lid, vent, bake 20 min hot then 45 min moderate
Fill @all-butter pie crust{1%recipe}(one 12-in round in a 9-in plate, one for the lid) with @&(~1)apple filling{}, lid it, crimp, cut four vents, brush with @heavy cream{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and scatter @coarse sugar{1%Tbs}(12 g), then ~bake{20%min} at 425°F (220°C) and ~bake{45%min} at 350°F (175°C).

>> step: cool 4 hours before it is cut
Cool @&(~1)baked pie{} on a rack ~cool{4%hr}.
